# LoRA adapter weights: 42 MB per checkpoint, ~650 MB across the two 23-db
# runs. Each file is under GitHub's 100 MB hard limit, so nothing stops a
# stray `git add -A` from permanently adding all of them. The sibling
# adapter_config.json files are NOT ignored and stay tracked -- the config
# is what makes a run reproducible; the weights are reproducible FROM it
# via `mlx_lm.lora --config fine_tuning/lora_config_23db_1000iter.yaml`.
# fine_tuning/adapters/ (the first, 6-db run) already has five .safetensors
# in published history; those stay -- this only stops adding more.
fine_tuning/adapters*/*.safetensors
fine_tuning/adapters*/**/*.safetensors

# Written deliverables (capstone report / defense deck). Kept out of the
# public repo deliberately: they are large binaries that would add a full
# fresh copy to history on every revision, and this repo is the code and
# the results, not the write-up. Same call as the adapter weights above.
*.pptx
*.docx

# macOS
.DS_Store
